on model" type="1" show="0"/></SYMBOL><WIRE a="86,90" b="75,90"/><LABEL pos="75,90" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">CONDITIONED</LABEL><WIRE a="86,92" b="80,92"/><LABEL pos="80,92" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">RETURN</LABEL><WIRE a="98,83" b="98,78"/><LABEL pos="98,78" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">SUPPLY</LABEL><WIRE a="98,99" b="98,104"/><LABEL pos="98,104" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">RETURN</LABEL><SYMBOL pos="41,84" id="4" show_power="0" can_scale="0" scale_x="1" scale_y="1" part="0" rotate="0"><FIELD pos="-1.4,-6" value="Test point" description="Name" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-1.4,-8.4" value="TP1" description="Ref" type="0" show="1"/><FIELD pos="-1.4,-6" value="TinyCAD configurable educational equivalent" description="Simulation model" type="1" show="0"/></SYMBOL><WIRE a="40,84" b="40,89"/><LABEL pos="40,89" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">SENSOR</LABEL><SYMBOL pos="41,104" id="5" show_power="0" can_scale="0" scale_x="1" scale_y="1" part="0" rotate="0"><FIELD pos="-1.4,-6" value="Test point" description="Name" type="1" show="0"/><FIELD pos="-1.4,-8.4" value="TP2" description="Ref" type="0" show="1"/><FIELD pos="-1.4,-6" value="TinyCAD configurable educational equivalent" description="Simulation model" type="1" show="0"/></SYMBOL><WIRE a="40,104" b="40,109"/><LABEL pos="40,109" font="3" color="432D14" direction="3" style="0">CONDITIONED</LABEL><NOTE_TEXT a="7,4" b="233,16.6" font="4" color="432D14" style="4" fill="0" direction="3" border_style="0">P19 · Electronic measurement-chain documentation</NOTE_TEXT><NOTE_TEXT a="147,21" b="233,148" font="1" color="432D14" style="5" fill="2" direction="3" border_style="0">## Follow the system interfaces

**First-year degree · ages 18+**

A system diagram shows where signals enter, how they are conditioned and where the results are used. Labelled connections describe interfaces; physical and software behaviour need separate evidence.

### Your investigation

Follow each signal from source to destination. Mark the reference, expected voltage range, loading and useful test points. Explain how you would test each stage.

### This activity

Draw sensor, conditioning stage, recorder/controller and references. Annotate supply and test connections. Firmware, physical data acquisition and weather-station operation need other tools.

### Getting started

This is a connection-planning drawing. Follow each labelled net, identify the real terminals and add your bench measurements. No simulation is attached.



**Explain:** Use an equation, a truth table or a state sequence to justify your prediction. Include units and discuss the model assumptions.

Check the physical layout with your teacher before construction.</NOTE_TEXT></TinyCAD><DSNSETTINGS><SHOW_RULERS>1</SHOW_RULERS></DSNSETTINGS><NETLIST_TYPES><TYPE name="default"/></NETLIST_TYPES></TinyCADSheets>